  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/141f1a6e-e562-4ef4-b2de-ea965268a5e6-9895943.PNG\" style=\"width: 304px; height: 250px;\" />.</p><p>Force exerted by each ball is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;is momentum and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;is time.</p><p>So, for one ball&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, total force exerted by the balls on the wall is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>200</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></math>.</p>",
